它改变了感觉。

00:56:14.960 --> 00:56:16.000
But by the way, I don't remember.
但顺便说一句，我不记得了。

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:17.960
I'm so impressed by Ted's memory.
特德的记忆力给我留下了深刻的印象。

00:56:17.960 --> 00:56:20.599
I know, even though I'm a little loud boy.
我知道，尽管我是个有点吵闹的男孩。

00:56:20.599 --> 00:56:23.599
He remembers so much more than we do now at this age.
他的记忆力比我们这个年纪的人还要多。

00:56:23.599 --> 00:56:31.039
What we keep asking the question is, what we're seeing Ted's version of it or are we seeing the real story and Ted is telling?
我们一直在问的问题是，我们看到的是特德的版本，还是我们看到的是特德讲述的真实故事？

00:56:31.039 --> 00:56:31.880
Do you know what I'm saying?
你知道我在说什么吗？

00:56:31.880 --> 00:56:35.639
Oh yeah, I think it's Ted's version now.
哦，是的，我想现在是特德的版本了。

00:56:35.639 --> 00:56:37.840
I feel like I just ate a sandwich from this question.
我觉得我刚刚吃了一个三明治。

00:56:37.840 --> 00:56:39.840
I feel so high right now.
我现在感觉很高。

00:56:39.840 --> 00:56:41.840
What if we're all just existing with an intense room?
如果我们都住在一个紧张的房间里怎么办？

00:56:41.840 --> 00:56:43.440
It's just we're gonna keep unpacking this.
只是我们要继续拆开这个。

00:56:43.440 --> 00:56:44.440
So romantic.
太浪漫了。

00:56:44.440 --> 00:56:45.639
It's still romantic.
还是很浪漫的。

00:56:45.639 --> 00:56:52.360
The story is so romantic and it's seen through this lovely lens of let's also say a good man.
这个故事是如此浪漫，而且是通过这个可爱的镜头看到的，我们也可以说是一个好男人。

00:56:52.360 --> 00:57:08.199
I think that like we struggle right now to find good men on TV and this is a show about somebody who's legitimately looking And for his life partner, it's so pure and really sweet and like, he's a good guy doing his best and making mistakes along the way.
我认为，就像我们现在在电视上努力寻找好男人一样，这是一个关于一个正在合法寻找的人的节目，对于他的生活伴侣来说，它是如此纯洁，非常甜蜜，就像，他是一个尽自己最大努力并一路犯错误的好人。

00:57:08.199 --> 00:57:12.360
And that's something we don't get to see very much anymore in a comical way.
我们再也不会以滑稽的方式看到这种情况了。

00:57:12.360 --> 00:57:17.480
And I think it's not a surprise that people are still so drawn to the show so many years later.
我认为多年后人们仍然对这部剧如此着迷并不奇怪。

00:57:17.480 --> 00:57:23.239
That's what makes a show classic is really decent people doing their best and we get to laugh along.
这就是这部剧之所以成为经典的原因，那就是真正正派的人们尽了最大努力，我们也能一起开怀大笑。

00:57:23.239 --> 00:57:28.690
Welcome back to the show.
欢迎回到节目。

00:57:28.690 --> 00:57:30.090
We're wrapping things up for today.
我们今天的事情就这样结束了。

00:57:30.090 --> 00:57:34.650
We've had such a good time talking to our friend Gloria Calderon-Kellett.
我们和朋友格洛丽亚·卡尔德隆-凯利特交谈得很愉快。

00:57:34.650 --> 00:57:39.690
Gloria, what a treat to see you and hear from you and just spend this time together.
格洛丽亚，见到你、听到你的消息、一起度过这段时间真是一种享受。

00:57:39.690 --> 00:57:42.530
Thank you so much for being here.
非常感谢您来到这里。

00:57:42.530 --> 00:57:43.305
Likewise.
同样地。

00:57:43.305 --> 00:57:43.805
Yeah.
是的。

00:57:43.805 --> 00:57:47.679
As we like to do in what we call the C-block.
正如我们喜欢在 C 区所做的那样。

00:57:49.130 --> 00:57:51.471
I don't know why we do that, we just do it.
我不知道我们为什么要这么做，我们就是这么做。

00:57:51.471 --> 00:57:52.777
Thank you for coming in.
谢谢您的光临。

00:57:52.777 --> 00:57:53.277
ASMR.
ASMR。

00:57:54.329 --> 00:57:55.507
We like, that's right.
我们喜欢，就对了。

00:57:55.507 --> 00:57:56.203
That's right.
这是正确的。

00:57:56.203 --> 00:57:59.843
If people use this to fall asleep, I hope that that knocks them out.
如果人们用它来入睡，我希望这能让他们昏过去。

00:57:59.843 --> 00:58:02.466
But we like to read at the beginning of the show.
但我们喜欢在节目开始时阅读。

00:58:02.466 --> 00:58:05.089
We obviously like to play a voice note from fans.
我们显然喜欢播放粉丝的语音留言。

00:58:05.089 --> 00:58:08.889
And at the end of the show, we like to read a note that we've received.
在节目结束时，我们想读一下我们收到的一张便条。

00:58:08.889 --> 00:58:14.960
If you would like to write us or record a voice note, please go to how we made your mother.com H-W-M-Y-M.
如果您想给我们写信或录制语音留言，请访问我们如何制作您的 mother.com H-W-M-Y-M。

00:58:14.960 --> 00:58:17.100
Go to contact, follow the directions.
前往联系方式，按照指示进行操作。

00:58:17.100 --> 00:58:17.678
Very easy.
很容易。

00:58:17.678 --> 00:58:20.511
This is our favorite thing to hear from you guys.
这是我们最喜欢从你们那里听到的事情。

00:58:20.511 --> 00:58:27.796
What the show means to you, you know, anecdotes about your life, how the show has affected you, how it changed things for you.
这个节目对你意味着什么，你知道，关于你生活的轶事，这个节目如何影响你，它如何改变你的事情。

00:58:27.796 --> 00:58:28.489
Let us know.
让我们知道。

00:58:28.489 --> 00:58:30.455
That's part of this whole thing, it's here.
这是整个事情的一部分，就在这里。

00:58:30.455 --> 00:58:32.329
So, Glow is going to be our guest reader.
因此，Glow 将成为我们的客座读者。

00:58:32.329 --> 00:58:34.489
guest reader for this week.
本周的客座读者。

00:58:34.489 --> 00:58:36.409
So take it away, Gloria.
所以把它拿走吧，格洛丽亚。

00:58:36.409 --> 00:58:37.272
Very exciting.
非常令人兴奋。

00:58:37.272 --> 00:58:37.772
Okay.
好的。

00:58:37.772 --> 00:58:40.361
This comes from Jane from Honolulu, Aloha.
这是来自檀香山的简，阿罗哈。

00:58:40.361 --> 00:58:46.524
I just came across your podcast the last couple of weeks and have already finished the first season.
我最近几周才看到你的播客，并且已经完成了第一季。

00:58:46.524 --> 00:58:48.681
It's making me feel very nostalgic.
这让我感到非常怀旧。

00:58:48.681 --> 00:59:00.821
Although I must have watched your show when it first came out, my fond memories are of watching it a few years later with my two young sons, starting when they were probably four and six years old.
虽然我一定在你的节目第一次播出时就看过了，但我美好的回忆是几年后和我的两个年幼的儿子一起观看的，从他们可能四岁和六岁的时候开始。

00:59:00.630 --> 00:59:08.369
As a full-time working mom with a 40 to 60 minute commute to the kid's school and my office, the end of the day was exhausting.
作为一名全职妈妈，每天要花 40 到 60 分钟通勤才能到达孩子的学校和我的办公室，一天结束时我感到筋疲力尽。

00:59:08.369 --> 00:59:17.289
After some time an hour in traffic, it was shuffling kids and all their things into the house, making dinner while helping with homework, washing dishes, and cleaning up.
经过一个小时的交通堵塞后，孩子们和他们所有的东西都拖着进屋，一边做晚饭，一边帮忙做作业、洗碗和打扫卫生。

00:59:17.289 --> 00:59:21.869
Then the three of us would plop down on the couch and watch how I met your mother.
然后我们三个人就会扑通一声坐在沙发上，看我是如何认识你母亲的。

00:59:21.869 --> 00:59:23.969
They were too young to understand all the jokes.
他们还太小，无法理解所有的笑话。

00:59:23.969 --> 00:59:27.409
Yes, but they loved the show anyway.
是的，但无论如何他们都很喜欢这个节目。

00:59:27.409 --> 00:59:31.050
and I love how time slowed down while we watched.
我喜欢我们观看时时间变慢的感觉。

00:59:31.050 --> 00:59:39.929
With my youngest sitting snuggly in my lap and my oldest cuddled up next to me, it was my half hour of adult time that the kids took part in.
我最小的孩子舒服地坐在我的腿上，最大的孩子依偎在我旁边，孩子们参与了我的半小时成人时间。

00:59:39.929 --> 00:59:47.409
After the show was over, the TV would go off and it was back to racing around for bath time, teeth brushing, books before bed and settling down.
演出结束后，电视就会关闭，人们又开始忙着洗澡、刷牙、睡前读书，然后安顿下来。

00:59:47.409 --> 00:59:57.369
Watching the show, there were probably a few times where I had to cover their eyes, but for the most part, it gave me the chance to explain things like, Bernie is showing how not to be.
看节目时，可能有几次我不得不遮住他们的眼睛，但在大多数情况下，这让我有机会解释诸如“伯尼正在展示如何不这样做”之类的事情。

00:59:57.369 --> 01:00:02.610
I was pleased when my friend said, he wanted to be just like Marshall and Lily when he.
当我的朋友说他想成为像马歇尔和莉莉那样的人时，我很高兴。

01:00:04.239 --> 01:00:10.239
As they got older, we continued to watch on the couch, sometimes binge watching during a rainstorm or a sick day.
随着他们年龄的增长，我们继续在沙发上观看，有时在暴雨或生病的日子里狂看。

01:00:10.239 --> 01:00:16.360
Soon they were teenagers who came and went, so I would sit on the couch and watch an episode or two by myself.
很快他们就变成了来来往往的青少年，所以我会坐在沙发上自己看一两集。

01:00:16.360 --> 01:00:31.320
In passing, they'd often ask, which one I was watching and all I'd have to say was a word or phrase like snowstorm or boats, boats, boats, and they'd know, I mean, sometimes if we were bored, I'd say, give me two numbers, and they'd randomly pick two numbers.
顺便说一句，他们经常会问，我在看哪一个，我只需说一个词或短语，比如暴风雪或船、船、船，他们就会知道，我的意思是，有时如果我们感到无聊，我会说，给我两个数字，他们会随机选择两个数字。

01:00:31.320 --> 01:00:36.880
First one for season, the second one for episode, and we'd watch that episode together now.
第一季的第一集，第二集的剧集，我们现在会一起观看这一集。

01:00:36.880 --> 01:00:38.900
You would be a good one.
你会是一个好人。

01:00:38.900 --> 01:00:43.900
Now my oldest is away on the mainland at college, and I'm starting to feel the dread of an empty nest.
现在我的大儿子远赴大陆上大学，我开始感受到空巢的恐惧。

01:00:43.900 --> 01:00:52.099
My youngest is not so young anymore, but will sit and watch with me as a happy palate cleanser after watching something scary or dark before bed.
我最小的孩子不再那么年轻了，但在睡前看了一些恐怖或黑暗的东西后，他会坐在我身边，作为快乐的味觉清洁剂。

01:00:52.099 --> 01:00:56.579
My oldest recently texted me a photo of himself in a suit for a kid who grew up in Hawaii.
我最大的孩子最近给我发了一张他穿着西装的照片，照片上是一个在夏威夷长大的孩子。

01:00:56.579 --> 01:01:00.219
It's not something you see before making a presentation.
这不是您在进行演示之前看到的东西。

01:01:00.219 --> 01:01:04.139
And I had this sincerest pleasure of texting back, you suit it up.
我很高兴能回复短信，你适合吧。

01:01:04.139 --> 01:01:14.980
I will forever equate how I met your mother with the feeling of sitting with my boys, laughing together, sometimes crying together and being present with each other to enjoy 20 minutes of stillness.
我将永远把我与你母亲的相遇等同于和我的孩子们坐在一起，一起笑，有时一起哭，彼此在一起享受 20 分钟宁静的感觉。

01:01:14.980 --> 01:01:28.821
I was lucky to have many of these moments throughout their childhood where I could marvel the observations of a five-year-old and then nine-year-old, then a teenager with some shows sparking conversation and some inspiring contemplation.
我很幸运，在他们的童年时期经历了很多这样的时刻，我可以惊叹一个五岁孩子、然后是九岁孩子、然后是一个十几岁孩子的观察，其中一些节目引发了对话和一些鼓舞人心的沉思。

01:01:28.821 --> 01:01:39.859
I'm hopeful that when both my kids are fully grown adults and I'm an wrinkly old woman, I'll be able to call or text them wherever they are and say, zitch dog or thank you Linus or suit up.
我希望，当我的两个孩子都长大成人，而我是一个满脸皱纹的老妇人时，无论他们身在何处，我都能够给他们打电话或发短信说，“zitch dogs”或者“谢谢你，Linus”或者穿好衣服。

01:01:39.859 --> 01:01:42.019
And they'll know exactly what I mean.
他们会确切地明白我的意思。

01:01:42.739 --> 01:01:43.714
Oh my gosh, wow.
天哪，哇。

01:01:43.714 --> 01:01:44.993
That's really moving.
这真是令人感动。

01:01:44.993 --> 01:01:50.780
I find that very moving because that letter covers like the huge span of time in and of itself.
我觉得这非常令人感动，因为这封信本身就涵盖了漫长的时间跨度。

01:01:50.780 --> 01:01:52.139
She took us on a journey.
她带我们去旅行。

01:01:52.139 --> 01:01:53.380
She took us on a journey.
她带我们去旅行。

01:01:53.380 --> 01:01:54.820
That was really well done.
那确实做得很好。

01:01:54.820 --> 01:01:55.659
That was a great letter.
那是一封很棒的信。

01:01:55.659 --> 01:01:56.219
Thank you.
谢谢。

01:01:56.219 --> 01:01:58.340
I feel the weight of the journey there.
我感受到了那里旅程的沉重。

01:01:58.340 --> 01:02:00.780
I love him Yem Roolette.
我爱他耶姆·鲁莱特。

01:02:00.780 --> 01:02:01.739
Like just call it out.
就像直接喊出来一样。

01:02:01.739 --> 01:02:04.940
Just call it out and just let in the face to side.
只要喊出来，然后让脸转向侧面即可。

01:02:04.940 --> 01:02:05.980
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

01:02:05.980 --> 01:02:06.900
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

01:02:06.900 --> 01:02:13.300
I also just, you know, kind of what we're doing, like growing older with a piece of art, you know, kind of alongside you.
我也只是，你知道，我们正在做的事情，就像随着一件艺术品一起变老，你知道，有点像在你身边。

01:02:13.300 --> 01:02:24.579
And as an access point to bond with your kids, My son watches the show with us occasionally, also far too young, six people, I don't think he should be watching it.
作为与孩子建立联系的一个切入点，我儿子偶尔会和我们一起看这个节目，他也太小了，六个人，我认为他不应该看。

01:02:24.579 --> 01:02:28.340
But he does, when I talk, he kind of his attention drifts.
但他确实如此，当我说话时，他的注意力有点转移。

01:02:28.340 --> 01:02:30.019
He knows that voice.
他认识那个声音。

01:02:30.019 --> 01:02:30.980
He knows that voice.
他认识那个声音。

01:02:30.980 --> 01:02:31.739
That's very cool.
太酷了。

01:02:31.739 --> 01:02:33.300
Yeah, that's very cool.
是的，那太酷了。

01:02:33.300 --> 01:02:39.460
Which is funny because I remember the reason they wouldn't let me do the narrators because they thought my voice didn't sound old enough.
这很有趣，因为我记得他们不让我担任旁白的原因是因为他们认为我的声音听起来不够老。

01:02:39.460 --> 01:02:39.980
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

01:02:39.980 --> 01:02:43.460
But I think my voice sounds somewhat similar to how it sounded.
但我觉得我的声音听起来和听起来有些相似。

01:02:43.460 --> 01:02:45.139
Your voice sounds exactly the same.
你的声音听起来一模一样。

01:02:45.139 --> 01:02:46.139
Yeah.
是的。

01:02:46.139 --> 01:02:48.596
Yeah, well, that was a lovely letter.
是的，那是一封可爱的信。

01:02:48.596 --> 01:02:52.380
Thank you so much and thank you to Gloria for being here.
非常感谢你们，也感谢格洛丽亚来到这里。

01:02:53.260 --> 01:02:54.042
Thank you, Glo.
谢谢你，格洛。

01:02:54.042 --> 01:02:58.059
Just wonderful to see you and what a great episode, how we met everyone else.
很高兴见到你，这是多么精彩的一集，我们是如何认识其他人的。

01:02:59.260 --> 01:03:00.539
And we'll see you next time.
我们下次再见。

